          "python",
          "PCA collapses 64 dimensions to 2, inevitably losing information. Still, the visualization reveals how SVMs create boundaries: smooth, non-linear curves separating classes. The black decision boundary (where the function equals zero) is what matters; regions far from it have high confidence predictions.\n\n## Multi-Class Strategy and Confusion Matrix\n\nSVMs are binary classifiers by design. Sklearn's one-vs-rest strategy: train 10 binary SVMs (digit 0 vs all, digit 1 vs all, ..., digit 9 vs all). For each test sample, all 10 models vote; the highest-confidence class wins."
